instructions:
Repository: /luxon (the luxon JS date library, version 1.20.0). Work only inside /luxon. You may run bash there (node, npx jest, npx prettier are available; node_modules is installed).

GOAL: Fix a bug in /luxon/src/interval.js in the static method `Interval.fromISO`.

BUG: When `Settings.throwOnInvalid` is true, `DateTime.fromISO(...)` THROWS an InvalidDateTimeError for a string that is not a date (e.g. the duration part "P1Y2M10DT2H30M"), so `Interval.fromISO("2007-03-01T13:00:00/P1Y2M10DT2H30M")` throws instead of returning a valid Interval. Similarly `Interval.fromISO("hello")` throws InvalidDateTimeError instead of InvalidIntervalError. The current code is:

```js
  static fromISO(text, opts) {
    const [s, e] = (text || "").split("/", 2);
    if (s && e) {
      const start = DateTime.fromISO(s, opts),
        end = DateTime.fromISO(e, opts);

      if (start.isValid && end.isValid) {
        return Interval.fromDateTimes(start, end);
      }

      if (start.isValid) {
        const dur = Duration.fromISO(e, opts);
        if (dur.isValid) {
          return Interval.after(start, dur);
        }
      } else if (end.isValid) {
        const dur = Duration.fromISO(s, opts);
        if (dur.isValid) {
          return Interval.before(end, dur);
        }
      }
    }
    return Interval.invalid("unparsable", `the input "${text}" can't be parsed asISO 8601`);
  }
```

REQUIRED FIX (replace the body of fromISO with exactly this, keeping the surrounding JSDoc comment untouched):

```js
  static fromISO(text, opts) {
    const [s, e] = (text || "").split("/", 2);
    if (s && e) {
      let start, startIsValid;
      try {
        start = DateTime.fromISO(s, opts);
        startIsValid = start.isValid;
      } catch (e) {
        startIsValid = false;
      }

      let end, endIsValid;
      try {
        end = DateTime.fromISO(e, opts);
        endIsValid = end.isValid;
      } catch (e) {
        endIsValid = false;
      }

      if (startIsValid && endIsValid) {
        return Interval.fromDateTimes(start, end);
      }

      if (startIsValid) {
        const dur = Duration.fromISO(e, opts);
        if (dur.isValid) {
          return Interval.after(start, dur);
        }
      } else if (endIsValid) {
        const dur = Duration.fromISO(s, opts);
        if (dur.isValid) {
          return Interval.before(end, dur);
        }
      }
    }
    return Interval.invalid("unparsable", `the input "${text}" can't be parsed as ISO 8601`);
  }
```

Note the second change: the error message typo `asISO 8601` must become `as ISO 8601`.

STEPS (do them in this order and report the results):
1. Baseline: `cd /luxon && npx jest 2>&1 | tail -60` — record the list of failing tests BEFORE any edit (there may be none).
2. Apply the edit to /luxon/src/interval.js with edit_file.
3. Verify formatting: `cd /luxon && npx prettier --check src/interval.js` (if it fails, run `npx prettier --write src/interval.js`).
4. Run `cd /luxon && npx jest test/interval 2>&1 | tail -40` and then the full `npx jest 2>&1 | tail -60`.
5. Write a temporary verification script /tmp/verify_interval.mjs or use `npx babel-node -e '...'` to check, with `Settings.throwOnInvalid = true`:
   - `Interval.fromISO("2007-03-01T13:00:00/P1Y2M10DT2H30M")` returns a valid Interval (start 2007-03-01T13:00:00, end 2008-05-11T15:30:00).
   - `Interval.fromISO("P1Y2M10DT2H30M/2008-05-11T15:30:00")` returns a valid Interval.
   - `Interval.fromISO("hello")` throws an error whose name/class is InvalidIntervalError (not InvalidDateTimeError).
   - With throwOnInvalid false, all the pre-existing behaviours of test/interval/parse.test.js still hold (bad inputs give invalidReason "unparsable").
   Delete the temp script afterwards.

CONSTRAINTS: Do NOT modify any file under /luxon/test. Do NOT change anything else in the repository (no other files, no reformatting of unrelated code, no git commits/checkouts/stashes).

REPORT: the exact baseline failing test list, the exact final failing test list, whether any test that passed at baseline now fails, the results of the step-5 checks, and the final content of the fromISO method.

