instructions:
Repository: /luxon (luxon JS date library v1.20.0). Work ONLY inside /luxon. You have bash (node, npx jest, npx babel-node; node_modules installed).

GOAL: Fix an injected bug in /luxon/src/datetime.js so that the hidden test `DateTime#isInDST() returns true for 1974 whole year in USA- from January 6th to October 27th` passes. Context: in 1974 the USA observed year-round DST (DST from Jan 6 to Oct 27, 1974). The current implementation of the `isInDST` getter in /luxon/src/datetime.js (~line 1164) is:

```js
  get isInDST() {
    if (this.isOffsetFixed) {
      return false;
    } else {
      return (
        this.offset > this.set({ month: 1 }).offset || this.offset > this.set({ month: 5 }).offset
      );
    }
  }
```

For a date in January 1974 (e.g. 1974-01-10 in America/New_York) `this.set({month: 1})` stays in January, which is already DST in 1974, so the comparison is equal and isInDST wrongly returns false. The correct behaviour is that any date in the DST period of the year is reported as DST, i.e. compare against a known-standard-time reference within the same year: `this.set({ month: 1, day: 1 })` (Jan 1 is standard time in the USA in 1974).

REQUIRED FIX: change the first comparison in `isInDST` from `this.set({ month: 1 }).offset` to `this.set({ month: 1, day: 1 }).offset`, keeping everything else identical:

```js
  get isInDST() {
    if (this.isOffsetFixed) {
      return false;
    } else {
      return (
        this.offset > this.set({ month: 1, day: 1 }).offset ||
        this.offset > this.set({ month: 5 }).offset
      );
    }
  }
```

STEPS:
1. Baseline: `cd /luxon && npx jest 2>&1 | tail -25`. Known pre-existing failures that MUST remain the only failures: 2 tests in test/datetime/toFormat.test.js (`DateTime#toFormat('FFF') returns a medium date/time representation without seconds` and `DateTime#toFormat('FFFF') ...`).
2. First PROVE the bug with a temp babel-node script created inside /luxon (e.g. /luxon/tmp_dst.js; babel-node only compiles files under cwd; delete it afterwards). Check with `Settings.defaultZoneName = "America/New_York"` (or setZone):
   - 1974-01-10, 1974-06-01, 1974-10-20 → isInDST must be true
   - 1974-01-03, 1974-11-15, 1974-12-01 → isInDST must be false
   - 2016-01-15 → false, 2016-06-15 → true, 2016-11-15 → false
   - 1974-01-06T03:00 (after the 2am switch) → true; 1974-01-06T01:00 → false
   Print the offsets too so the reasoning is verifiable.
3. Apply the fix with edit_file (only that getter, no reformatting of anything else).
4. Re-run the probe script and confirm all the above expectations hold.
5. Run `cd /luxon && npx jest test/datetime 2>&1 | tail -30` and the full `npx jest 2>&1 | tail -25`; confirm the failing set is unchanged from baseline (only the 2 ICU toFormat tests). Also run `npx prettier --list-different src/datetime.js` (must print nothing).
6. Run `git diff` in /luxon and report it.

CONSTRAINTS: Do NOT modify anything under /luxon/test. Do NOT modify /luxon/src/impl/util.js (another agent is editing it concurrently) or /luxon/src/interval.js or /luxon/src/duration.js. Do not run git commit/checkout/stash/restore.

